145		The win predicate $D^{\mathrm{ld}} = D^{\mathrm{ld}}_{\mathsf{ldparams}}$ is the function of the tuple $(t_{\mathrm A}, x_{\mathrm A}, t_{\mathrm B}, x_{\mathrm B}, a_{\mathrm A}, a_{\mathrm B})$ determined by the following clauses, evaluated for $w \in \{\mathrm A,\mathrm B\}$; in all cases where no action is indicated, the predicate accepts.
146		\begin{enumerate}
147			\item (\textbf{Consistency test}) If $t_{\mathrm A} = t_{\mathrm B}$, accept if and only if $a_{\mathrm A} = a_{\mathrm B}$.
